/-!
# Global generation of `ω_X|_E` from duality at the canonical dualizing sheaf

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] with `A` not regular, let `X` be the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the
maximal ideal, `i : E ⟶ X` its exceptional divisor and `ω_X` a coherent module on `X`. Clause (3)
of [Stacks, Tag 0B64] takes as its one input the global generation of `ω_X|_E`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] at `E` over the residue field `κ`.

`…/RationalSingularities/ExceptionalDualizingGeneration.lean` performs that application at the
shape of [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] which leaves `ω_E` a free parameter, and so carries the five inputs
`hdual`, `hone`, `hnosub`, `hd`, `hsec` of it; of those, `hsec` is **unsatisfiable** over a
residue field that is not algebraically closed, so that route cannot reach the conclusion. This
file takes the other route — the one the source itself takes — and applies
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] *at the canonical dualizing sheaf* `Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField` of
`E ⟶ Spec(κ)`, where all five are proved, over an arbitrary `κ`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation`
`.nonempty_generatingSections_dualizing_tensorSheaf_of_isoAlgebraicClosure` of
`…/Curves/VanishingResults/DualizingTwistGenerationGeneralField.lean`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
  `.nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_isoDualizingSheaf`: `ω_X|_E` is generated by its
  global sections, granted two isomorphisms.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_dualizingPullbackMap_of_isoDualizingSheaf`: **clause (3)
  of [Stacks, Tag 0B64]** granted the same two isomorphisms, and nothing else.

## The two isomorphisms, and why they are the whole remaining distance

`hsec` does not appear here, nor does any hypothesis on the residue field. What is carried instead
is two isomorphisms, each a true statement of the source:

* `ecan`, that `ω_E = H¹(a(ω_X))` — the module clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64] identifies with
  `(ω_X|_E)(-1)`, `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.exceptionalDualizingModule` — **is** the
  dualizing sheaf of `E` as a proper curve over `κ`. Being *a* dualizing module is not enough:
  by [Stacks, Tag 0A7F] a dualizing complex is unique only up to shift and invertible twist, and
  neither the duality of clause (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2] nor `dim_κ H¹(E, ω_E) = 1` is
  twist-invariant. The source obtains it by propagating the normalization of
  [Stacks, Remark 0B4R] along `f` and `i`. All three steps of that propagation are proved
  separately — [Stacks, Tag 0ATX] as `Stacks.Duality.twistedInverseImageCompIso`, the right
  adjoint at `Spec(κ) ⟶ Spec(A)` as `R Hom_A(κ, -)` by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.twistedInverseImage_residuePoint_isoDerivedHom` (which is
  [Stacks, Tag 0A9F] at the twisted inverse image, not [Stacks, Tag 0AA2]: `j` is affine), and
  the cohomological reading of [Stacks, Tag 0A7M] as
  `Dualizing.subsingleton_ext_residueField_single_of_ne_localRingDimension` — and `ecan` is
  spliced, as `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation`
  `.nonempty_homologyOne_twistedInverseImage_iso_dualizingSheaf_of_dualizingNormalization` of
  `…/RationalSingularities/ExceptionalDualizingSheafNormalized.lean`. That splice reads `H¹` of
  the [Stacks, Tag 0A9E] right adjoint at `i`, at the locally small model, where `H¹(a(ω_X))` is
  derived sheaf Hom at `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`, and identifying those two is
  [Stacks, Tag 0A9X] at the locally small model,
  `Stacks.Duality.isDerivedSheafHomRightAdjoint_twistedInverseImage` of
  `…/Duality/ClosedImmersionRightAdjointLocallySmall.lean`. With it `ecan` is proved as
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
  `.nonempty_exceptionalDualizingModule_iso_dualizingSheafOverField` of
  `…/Duality/ExceptionalDualizingSheafIdentification.lean`, where clause (2) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0B64] is registered with nothing left over. It stays an explicit input below only
  because the statement below takes the degree-zero condition `NormalizedDualizingModule`, where
  the splice needs `ω_X` normalized in the sense of [Stacks, Remark 0B4R]
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.DualizingNormalization`), the implication not
  reversing.
* `e0E32`, [Stacks, Tag 0E32] at `E`: the inverse image of the dualizing sheaf along
  `E_{κ̄} ⟶ E` is the dualizing sheaf of the base change. This is the one input of the source's
  reduction of [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] to an algebraically closed base field that this development
  lacks; it rests on [Stacks, Tag 0AA8], which is registered nowhere here, and thence on the
  invertibility of the pushforward comparison `ξ` of [Stacks, Tag 0A9K]. That invertibility *is*
  proved — `Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion`
  `.isIso_twistedInverseImagePushforwardBaseChange_of_isOpenImmersion` of
  `…/Duality/OpenImmersion/TwistedInverseImageRestrictionBaseChange.lean`, and
  `Stacks.Duality.isIso_refinementXi` for a compactification square — but only when the base
  change morphism is an open immersion, and `E_{κ̄} ⟶ E` is a field extension, not one; the
  general Tor-independent case is what that file records as not proved. See the module
  documentation of `…/Curves/VanishingResults/DualizingTwistGenerationGeneralField.lean`.

Everything else at `E` is discharged. Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] at `E` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor`, hypothesis-free; very ampleness
of `𝒪_E(1)` is clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0B63]; the degree bound `deg 𝒪_E(1) ≥ 2` is clause (3)
of that tag together with the non-regularity of `A`, which is
`…two_le_invertibleCurveDegree_curveTwistSheaf_one`; the identification of `ω_X|_E` with
`ω_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(1)` is clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64], proved and *not* carried here; and the
quasi-coherence and finite type of `ω_X|_E` come from coherence of `ω_X`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached, because two hypotheses are carried.

## References

